<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vita Karoli Magni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 817–830</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Life of Charlemagne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vita Karoli Magni, or Life of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, is a biography of the Frankish emperor written by his courtier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/einhard">Einhard</a>, probably in the 820s. Modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suetonius">Suetonius</a>' lives of the Roman emperors, it describes Charlemagne's wars, character, family and habits. It is the most important contemporary account of Charlemagne and became a model for later medieval royal biography.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vita-karoli-magni.jpg" alt="Vita Karoli Magni" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eginhard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89ginhard_Vita_Caroli_magni_imperatoris-Lettrine_V_histori%C3%A9e_Charlemagne_assis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
